{
    "background_story": "Lover was a majestic chestnut gelding with a shiny coat and a spirited personality. However, beneath his athletic exterior, Lover had a secret: he was born with a rare heart condition known as pericardial effusion. Despite this, he had a remarkable ability to adapt and thrive. With careful management and regular veterinary check-ups, Lover learned to navigate his limitations and still excel in the show jumping arena. His rider, a skilled and patient young woman named Sarah, worked tirelessly with Lover to build his strength and endurance. Together, they formed an unbreakable bond, with Lover's loyalty and trust in Sarah inspiring her to push beyond her own limits. As they soared over obstacles, Lover's pericardial condition became a reminder that even the most fragile hearts can achieve greatness with the right care and devotion.",
